    "### Client B — Holy Grail diversification\n",
    "\n",
    "**Why these stocks?** Our client wants a steady portfolio in Canadian dollars. We use Ray Dalio’s Holy Grail idea: hold stocks that do not all move together. We try three starting stocks with low daily volatility. At each step we test every remaining stock with the current basket on the same dates. We give priority to having enough room under the sector and stock limits. We then choose the addition with the lowest combined volatility at equal initial weights. This measure reflects both the stock’s own risk and how it moves with our holdings.\n",
    "\n",
    "**How much do we invest?** For each feasible basket of 10–20 stocks, we test equal starting amounts and inverse-volatility weights. The second rule gives less money to more volatile stocks. We cap sectors and individual positions, keep the lowest historical volatility we find and test one round of single-stock replacements. This is a simple search, so another combination could do better.\n",
    "\n",
